  {
   "id": "ToUO1iqmAgAJ",
   "from": "Lucía Rodríguez Planes",
   "author": "1759d327a50679e2",
   "date": "2020-06-26T18:25:14Z",
   "subject": "Re: [camtrapR] metadata tagging in digiKam",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Mari! In my experience it&#39;s better to put each variable as a different label. That&#39;s because later when reading into R those labels, each one becomes a column in a data frame. The inner hierarchy of each label becomes the different levels on that categorical variable. For example, I usually do it this way for the label &quot;number of individuals&quot; with an inner hierarchy &quot;1&quot;, &quot;2&quot;, &quot;3&quot;, ... Hope this helps!</div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br></div><div>Lucía RP</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">El jue., 25 jun. 2020 a las 8:48, Mari Piñero Rodríguez (&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mari....@gmail.com</a>&gt;) escribió:<br></div></div>"
    ],
